From c4b5e1dc794318cf67bce93fbbe0517d22053dff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:53:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 108/113] drm/evdi: add the Rust virtual display driver

Add a Rust implementation of EVDI while preserving the existing libevdi and
DisplayLinkManager ABI. Create devices through the established sysfs
interface, expose the expected ioctls and events, and remove each card with
its associated USB device.

Use owned DRM, KMS, USB, event, and sysfs abstractions. Connector state,
CRTC handles, event payloads, USB notifications, and buffer access remain
within the safe interfaces supplied by the preceding patches.

Prepare a bounded four-entry scanout pool with owned shmem mappings. Map
compositor swapchain buffers before notifying the client. Reuse them for
later flips and GRABPIX calls, and release them on DPMS-off or teardown.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
